      "topic": "staff",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 27,
      "title": {
        "en": "Attentive clinicians with mixed front desk reviews"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Many reviewers commend Dr V, Dr Keene, and Dr Molena for saving critically ill animals and providing compassionate care. Clients appreciate that doctors explain complex diagnoses with patience and dedication. However, several pet owners express dissatisfaction with rude receptionists and disjointed handoffs at the front desk."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 15,
      "title": {
        "en": "Triage and care for acute emergencies"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients bring pets with acute trauma, toxicity, and severe illnesses, praising the team's readiness to triage critical patients. Reviewers note that staff handle stressed dogs and cats with reassurance during urgent evaluations. While one owner felt their cat was handled roughly, most describe comforting care during emergencies."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "prices",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 12,
      "title": {
        "en": "Accessible and budget-conscious emergency care"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners widely praise the practice for offering substantially lower fees than corporate emergency facilities in San Diego. Clients appreciate that staff avoid unnecessary diagnostic upsells and accommodate limited budgets. Nonetheless, a minority of reviewers report upfront deposit disputes and surrender pressures during crises."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
